# ExtendScript Gotchas (After Effects)

ExtendScript is **ES3**. These are critical constraints — don't repeat them.

## No JSON object
```javascript
// WRONG — JSON is undefined in ExtendScript
return JSON.stringify({ success: true, message: msg });
```
```javascript
// CORRECT — use the respond() helper (included in every .jsx file)
return respond(true, msg);
```

## No ES5+ syntax or methods
No `forEach`, `map`, `filter`, `indexOf`, `trim`, arrow functions, `const`, `let`, template literals, or destructuring. Use `for` loops and `var` only.

## Always use undo groups
Wrap any state-changing operation in `app.beginUndoGroup()` / `app.endUndoGroup()` so users get a single Cmd+Z.

## Check for active composition
```javascript
// CORRECT — always guard against no active comp
var comp = app.project.activeItem;
if (!comp || !(comp instanceof CompItem)) {
  return respond(false, 'No active composition.');
}
```

## Position values can be 2D or 3D
After Effects layers can have 2D `[x, y]` or 3D `[x, y, z]` position. Always check `.length`:
```javascript
var pos = layer.property('Position').value;
if (pos.length === 3) {
  layer.property('Position').setValue([newX, newY, pos[2]]);
} else {
  layer.property('Position').setValue([newX, newY]);
}
```

## Property access via strings
Use `layer.property('Position')` not `layer.position` for setting values. String-based access is safer and works across all layer types.

## Layer indices are 1-based
`comp.layer(1)` is the first layer, not `comp.layer(0)`. `comp.numLayers` gives the count.

## Color values are 0–1 floats
After Effects uses `[r, g, b]` with values from 0 to 1, not 0 to 255.

## Debugging
- Panel HTML/JS: Chrome at `localhost:8800` (or port from `.debug`)
- ExtendScript: ExtendScript Toolkit → attach to After Effects, use `$.writeln()` for logging
- Panel shows raw JSX return value on parse failures (`JSX error: ...`)
